.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 *
. 
.         *********************************************************************
> *******
.         *Verbal description of the model:       
.         * The gender gap in total labor contributions in the household 
.         * (measured as the absolute difference in reported hours spent on pai
> d and 
.         * unpaid work between male and female partners, sum of the variables:
>  
.         * pli0040 pli0046 pli0051 pli0043_h pli0049_h pli0044_h plb0186_h) 
.         * is used as a proxy for gender equality in the household (hypothesis
>  3). 
.         * Smaller time-use gaps (higher values) between women and men indicat
> e a 
.         * more equal sharing of responsibilities.
.         
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with the chang
> e score 
.         * of the gender time-use gap between survey waves (variable: timeused
> iff) 
.         * as the dependent variable, and the dummy variable daughter as the 
.         * independent variable. 
.         * We further control for age of both partners (variables: age_women a
> ge_men) 
.         * and survey year (variable: syear) in the model. 
.         * We estimate cluster-robust standard errors (cluster variable: pid).
>  
.         * The regression is weighted (weight: phrf).
.         *********************************************************************
> *******
. 
.         reg timeusediff i.daughter age_women age_men i.syear [aw=phrf], clust
> er(pid)
(sum of wgt is 12,252,209.11)

